On 3 Nov 1999 Toni Harbaugh-Blackford wrote:

> Does anyone have patches that will allow vmubc to compile on Tru64 v5.0 ?

It compiles just fine, but dies with message

  kmem - cannot read machine_slot

Vmubc (in file system.c) uses nlist() to look up addresses in kmem for:

  machine_slot
  ubc_dirtypages
  ubc_maxpages
  ubc_minpages
  ubc_pages

but these are not available at V5. Which is rather odd: line 108 of file
/usr/include/mach/machine.h has "extern machine_slot_t *machine_slot;" but
still no /sys/BINARY/*.mod files have this (as an external symbol: used to
be defined in std_kern.mod, and 'strings -a' still shows it, but not 'nm').
The ubc variables are not declared external in /usr/include/sys/table.h or
/usr/sys/include/vm/vm_numa.h (this last file was not present at V4): it is
not surprising that they are not available.

The reason vmubc dies is that it has no error checks on the nlist() return
values: an address of zero is used in the kmem read, which fails. The best
I could do is to put in error checks for lookup failures. Then it cannot
show UBC things, nor usage for each CPU in a multi-CPU machine (that part
seems to work fine on a single-CPU machine as machine_slot is not used).

Paul Szabo - System Manager   //        School of Mathematics and Statistics
psz@maths.usyd.edu.au         //   University of Sydney, NSW 2006, Australia

