On Sat, 19 Feb 2000, Jonathan Nicholson wrote:

> 
> I just had an ADVFS file system go down because it couldn't read the last
> block of a volume in the domain.
> 
> The domain is made up of 2 disks rz9c & rz11c. rz9 is a partition of an
> HSZ50 raid 5 set and rz11 is a mirror set off the same hsz50.
> 
> Everything is redundant (dual hsz50 dual psu etc) and the disks are all
> mirrored/raid so what could have caused this?

This turned out to be because the disk label on the disk was incorrect.

The disk is presented to 2 nodes in an ASE cluster - the 2 nodes were
seeing different disk labels (presumably a stale entry from a previous
disk on the bus)

Zeroing & Re-labeling the disk (on both nodes!) seems to have fixed the
problem...

Regards,

Jonathan


