From tru64-unix-managers  Tue Feb 01 20:43:51 2000
From: Becki Kain <beckers () josephus ! furph ! com>
Date: Tue, 01 Feb 2000 20:43:51 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: {S} disklabel question
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079336919160

A very late summary.  My original question showed my disk label using -p
option (disklabel -p /dev/rrz0c) and all my partitions showed up as unused
and, in my eyes, not allocated properly.  The problem was the option, -r
(disklabel -r /dev/rrz0c) actually reads the label on the disk.  The -p
option just reads the /etc/disktab file.  

