Hello all!

I'm wondering if there's a way to enable the /proc filesystem under DU4.0d,
so that it contains information similar to that found under Linux?  Or, is
there another way to glean all of that information?

The /proc filesystem contains all sorts of information and stats regarding
memory, cpu, network, kernel, etc.  It can be used to tweak components of
the kernel such as packet forwarding, spoof protection, etc.  It can
probably be used for more as well - I just haven't discovered all that yet.
:)  The nice thing is, the info is in textfiles so it's easily readable.

Cheers!
Jon
