Stan Horwitz suggested to path my system to at least patch kit #3 because
of Y2K problems. i didn't do that yet.

Roger Leonard has the permissions 755 on the index-dirs. we got 700, but
all daemons run with root-priviliges and so permissions shouldn't be the
problem.

John Ziomek installed the patched releases of 5.5.1. we already installed
the patch and now have 5.5.1.Build.143 Turbo/4. the problem remained.

Tom Webster suggested to add 'localhost' to the servers resource-file
on the client and the server. i'll try that now and see what happended
in the next morning.

Tom also wrote, that only the bootstrap information are not saved.
apart from disaster recovery everything should work.

